 year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Kodiak has set <strong>70 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 89 that chance alone would give, and <strong>99 record highs</strong>, close to the 88 that chance alone would give. The 1980s hold the most record highs of any decade (41). Kodiak's all-time high is 86\u00b0F, on August 16, 2019.","t_chg":"Kodiak's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 101 complete years: Kodiak's average low shows no clear change: +0.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.04 to +0.17) that includes zero. Kodiak's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.29), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1916. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.49\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.89) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Kodiak has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Kodiak's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+2.50 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +1.57 to +3.42), about +27.0 inches since 1917. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 78.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1998 (106.25 in); the driest, 1972 (38.33 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows"}}